19b7cd082199eb5ee69e6ccad16653e953af3a83bd"} {"question" "q-106704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the point $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +h,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(3,-2),$ $a=3$ and $b=8.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/state.json" "file_sha256" "e525b3ca26f6e25cbdc38019b7cd082199eb5ee69e6ccad16653e953af3a83bd"} {"question" "q-106704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cd3c3ab57d3f4eee40fa133cc881384f001d3a25c4d860095ddb8674be6cfd87"} {"question" "q-106704" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/state.json" "file_sha256" "e525b3ca26f6e25cbdc38019b7cd082199eb5ee69e6ccad16653e953af3a83bd"} {"question" "q-106704" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2"] ["math" "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2"] ["math" "x=64\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2"] ["math" "x=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2"] ["math" "x=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/state.json" "file_sha256" "e525b3ca26f6e25cbdc38019b7cd082199eb5ee69e6ccad16653e953af3a83bd"} {"question" "q-106704" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/state.json" "file_sha256" "e525b3ca26f6e25cbdc38019b7cd082199eb5ee69e6ccad16653e953af3a83bd"} {"question" "q-327828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/assets/f29c8db431035fda7e50771b3baaf6d19f51a60e26582957bbff0f70dbfdc5ed.png)\n\nThe quarter-ellipse above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta ?$\n\n$\\theta \\in [${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/state.json" "file_sha256" "e525b3ca26f6e25cbdc38019b7cd082199eb5ee69e6ccad16653e953af3a83bd"} {"question" "q-327828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=6$ and $b=4.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the *full* ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-ellipse, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the ellipse and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/assets/24b56c8addea0d8a0f3effeeefc2788023c452e98b05d10db7893aeebde9ba5e.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$, we get the quarter-ellipse.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the quarter-ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/state.json" "file_sha256" "e525b3ca26f6e25cbdc38019b7cd082199eb5ee69e6ccad16653e953af3a83bd"} {"question" "q-327828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cd3c3ab57d3f4eee40fa133cc881384f001d3a25c4d860095ddb8674be6cfd87"} {"question" "q-327828" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/state.json" "file_sha256" "e525b3ca26f6e25cbdc38019b7cd082199eb5ee69e6ccad16653e953af3a83bd"} {"question" "q-327828" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/state.json" "file_sha256" "e525b3ca26f6e25cbdc38019b7cd082199eb5ee69e6ccad16653e953af3a83bd"} {"question" "q-327828" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004891/state.json" "file_sha256" "e525b3ca26f6e25cbdc38019b7cd082199eb5ee69e6ccad16653e953af3a83bd"} {"question" "q-327828" "field" "field-2" "at